course: dictionary
lesson: 4882
title: Idiotic and strong words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are strong. They tell you not just what someone thinks, but how hard they feel about it. Idiotic means very stupid or silly, so much that it makes no sense at all.
explain: Idiotic is informal and quite rude. We use it about an idea, a plan or a remark, not as a polite way to describe a person. Saying a plan is idiotic is harsh; saying it does not quite make sense is kinder.
explain: Read the clues around the word. In «calls him "perfectly idiotic"», the word perfectly makes the insult stronger. Ask yourself: would a polite person say this out loud? If not, the word is informal or rude, so think before you use it.
fact: Idiotic means very stupid or silly; making no sense.
fact: Idiotic is informal and quite rude, so use it carefully.
fact: Use idiotic about ideas, plans and remarks, not as a polite way to describe a person.
fact: «Perfectly idiotic» means completely silly, with the word perfectly making it stronger.
fact: In stories, characters often call Toad's schemes idiotic when they argue about them.
exercise: In «calls him "perfectly idiotic"», what does perfectly idiotic mean? | *Completely silly and making no sense | Perfectly clever and well planned | Kind and helpful to everyone | Lost in a forest
exercise: Which thing is best described as idiotic? | *A plan that makes no sense at all | A sunny day at the seaside | A kind friend who shares her lunch
exercise: Which word is a gentler choice than idiotic for a silly idea? | *Silly | Barely | Ancient | Idiotic
test: Toad's friends say his latest scheme is idiotic. What are they saying? | *The scheme is very stupid and makes no sense | The scheme is very old and dusty | The scheme is very clever and certain to work | The scheme is very quiet and gentle
test: Why is idiotic a strong word to use with care? | *It is informal and rude, so it can hurt feelings | It is a long word that means happy | It is a polite word that children use at school | It means very tired and sleepy
exam: Which is the kindest way to tell a friend that their plan is silly? | That plan is idiotic, and so are you | *That plan doesn't quite make sense to me | That plan is idiotic and everyone knows it
